{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0111GfgWVAnT3ZjWJ9m8bim9","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# OntoCoDec — Paper Framing\n2\t\n3\t## Target Venue\n4\tEMNLP 2026 (ARR submission May 25, 2026)\n5\t\n6\t## Title\n7\tOntoCoDec: Type-Valid Information Extraction via Compiled Ontology Constraints\n8\t(D015: \"Near-Complete\" dropped — DocRED residual DR=10.21% (Qwen) 不算 near-complete。论文贡献是方法，不是特定消除率。SciERC 0.93% 和 DocRED 2.55% (Llama) 可在正文中描述为 near-complete，但 title 不宜 overclaim。)\n9\t\n10\t## Core Insight\n11\tLLM-based IE systems produce systematic ontology constraint violations concentrated in specific relation types. Prompt-level intervention (schema-informed prompting) reduces violations by ~62% but cannot eliminate them — certain relation types retain 25-30% violation rates even with explicit constraint descriptions. OntoCoDec provides **near-complete elimination (DR 15.4%→0.93%, ↓94%) at zero or positive F1 impact** through automatic ontology-to-decoder constraint compilation with two complementary layers.\n12\t\n13\t**Phase 2 confirmed (D012 bootstrap CI, v2 fix)**: Grammar+Semantic dual-layer constrained decoding reduces domain/range violations by 94%, eliminates entity-type and relation-vocabulary violations entirely (→0%). F1 impact is **dataset-dependent**:\n14\t- SciERC: Rel F1 neutral (+0.13pp, p=0.58), Ent F1 neutral (-0.03pp, p=0.53)\n15\t- DocRED: Rel F1 **significantly improved** (+0.50pp, p<0.001, 95% CI [+0.23, +0.81]); Ent F1 **significantly improved** (+1.23pp, p<0.001, 95% CI [+0.94, +1.55])\n16\t- Mechanism: grammar 消除 OOV relation names (DocRED RV 29.66%→0.03%) + 非标 entity types (ET 2.48%→0%)。all_set F1 方法下 OOV=FP → fewer FP → higher precision/F1。SciERC baseline RV/ET 已很低，效果不显著。\n17\t- **Grammar 层是 F1 提升的唯一来源**: grammar_only Ent F1=59.38% ≈ full_s1 59.37% (Δ+0.01pp, p=0.66)。Semantic 层对 F1 无额外贡献，专注 DR reduction。\n18\t\n19\t## Core Claims\n20\t\n21\t### Claim 1 (Empirical): Violation Landscape\n22\tLLM-based IE systems violate ontology type constraints at non-trivial rates (15.4% per-triple on SciERC, 18.7% on DocRED). Violations are **not uniformly distributed** — they concentrate on relation types with tight domain/range constraints (Feature-of 33.5%, Compare 42.4%) while loose-constraint relations show near-zero violation (Used-for 0.8%).\n23\t\n24\t**Key insight**: Violation rate is driven by **constraint tightness**, not ontology size. A small ontology with tight constraints can produce more violations than a large ontology with loose constraints.\n25\t\n26\t**D014 修订**: DR reduction ceiling 由 **tightness × model RV baseline** 共同决定，非 tightness 单因素。Llama DocRED DR↓90.2% vs Qwen DR↓44.7%（同一 ontology τ̄=0.842）。机制：Qwen RV=29.66% >> Llama RV=16.03% → grammar 层将 OOV triples 强制匹配有效关系名 → 揭露大量 latent DR violations → 残余 DR 更高。这是比单一 tightness 更深的 insight。\n27\t\n28\t**Evidence**: SciERC (7 relations) 15.4%; DocRED (96 relations) 18.7% — comparable rates despite 14× ontology size difference. Schema-informed prompt on DocRED only achieves DR↓32% (vs SciERC ↓62%), confirming **prompt-level intervention scales poorly with ontology complexity**.\n29\t\n30\t### Claim 2 (Empirical): Prompt Insufficiency\n31\tSchema-informed prompting (explicitly describing domain/range constraints in the prompt) reduces but does not eliminate violations:\n32\t- Overall: 15.4% → 5.78% (-62.4%), still above 5%\n33\t- Per-relation: Compare 42.4% → 27.6%, Evaluate-for 24.1% → 29.9% (**worse**)\n34\t- Prompt intervention is unreliable at the per-relation level — some relations improve, one regresses\n35\t\n36\t**Narrative**: This is NOT about \"5.78% barely above 5%\". The story is: **prompt-level intervention is fundamentally unreliable as a guarantee mechanism**. It works statistically but cannot provide per-instance compliance. Three specific relation types retain >10% violation rates with schema-informed prompts. For safety-critical IE (biomedical, legal, regulatory), statistical reduction is insufficient — guaranteed compliance is required.\n37\t\n38\t### Claim 3 (Methodological): Composable Constraint Framework\n39\tOntoCoDec automatically compiles IE ontology schemas into two composable constraint layers:\n40\t1. **Grammar layer** (XGrammar): JSON structure + type vocabulary constraints (CFG-expressible)\n41\t2. **Semantic layer** (TypeConstraintProcessor): Cross-field domain/range constraints via stateful entity registry + dynamic logit masking\n42\t\n43\tThe two layers are **complementary with enabling dependency**: grammar ensures every generated relation type is in the valid vocabulary, which enables the semantic layer to look up and enforce domain/range rules for that type. Without grammar, the semantic layer encounters unknown relation types and cannot enforce constraints (explaining why semantic_only achieves only ↓24% vs full_s1 ↓94%). This is NOT \"synergistic\" (mutual amplification) — grammar is a prerequisite for semantic, not vice versa.\n44\t\n45\tThe two layers compose via bitwise AND of token masks. Recommended framing: \"Grammar and semantic constraints compose via bitwise AND with an enabling dependency: grammar ensures structural validity, enabling semantic constraints to enforce domain/range rules. When constraint tightness creates empty intersection between layers, the system degrades gracefully to grammar-only constraints, maintaining structural validity as a guaranteed floor.\"\n46\t\n47\t**Graceful degradation + Fallback 频率量化** (D008 + Reviewer 发现):\n48\tWhen $M_{semantic} \\cap M_{grammar} = \\emptyset$, the system falls back to grammar-only control.\n49\t\n50\t**关键量化数据（Reviewer 从日志挖掘）**:\n51\t- Llama DocRED full_s1: **32,921 次 fallback / 577 docs = ~57 次/doc**\n52\t- Llama SciERC full_s1: **5,882 次 fallback / 550 docs = ~10.7 次/doc**\n53\t- DocRED fallback 频率是 SciERC 的 **5.3×**\n54\t- Qwen DocRED fallback 率未知（日志当时无 fallback logging，需估算）\n55\t\n56\t**这直接解释了 DocRED DR 残余 10.19% vs SciERC 0.93%**: 更多 token 位置退化为 grammar-only → grammar-only 的 DR 已知为 26.17% → 高 fallback = 高残余 DR。\n57\t\n58\t**论文建议**: 在 §5 tightness 段报告 fallback 率，定义 \"Constraint Coverage\" 指标（semantic masking 实际生效的 token 比例）。这把 \"10.19% DR 残余\" 从弱点变成可量化分析的 finding。Frame as \"engineering robustness\" in §4; fallback 频率 + tightness 作为 §5 定量分析。\n59\t\n60\t**Decidability taxonomy**: Constraints classified by prefix-decidability:\n61\t- (a) Purely local: entity type ∈ vocabulary (grammar layer)\n62\t- (b) Prefix-decidable with state: relation argument types compatible with domain/range (semantic layer, requires entity registry)\n63\t- (c) Truly non-local: forward coreference — out of scope for forward-only decoding\n64\t\n65\t### Claim 4 (Methodological): S1 vs S2 Decoding Strategies — Architectural Ablation\n66\t- S1 (single-pass): Both layers applied throughout generation. **Recommended primary strategy** — simpler, slightly better metrics across the board.\n67\t- S2 (two-pass): Pass 1 extracts entities (grammar-only), Pass 2 generates relations with input-dependent grammar compiled from Pass 1 entities.\n68\t\n69\t**S2 full results (551/551 SciERC)**: DR 0.97% (vs S1 0.93%), CF 8.03% (vs S1 9.9%), R-F1 8.03% (vs S1 8.36%). S2 does NOT solve CF — the 1.87pp reduction is not significant. S2 also slightly worse on DR and F1. **S2 is an architectural variant demonstrating framework flexibility, not a CF solution.** Position in paper as ablation (Section 5 or Appendix), not as a core contribution.\n70\t\n71\t⚠️ **Do NOT cite pilot50 DR=0% as S2 evidence** — small-sample artifact; full run shows DR=0.97%. Per-relation S2 DR is worse than S1 on Compare (4.6% vs 2.82%), Part-of (1.25% vs 0%), Used-for (0.12% vs 0%).\n72\t\n73\t## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns\n74\t\n75\t### C1: \"5.78% is barely above 5% — threshold is arbitrary\"\n76\t**Response**: Don't argue about the threshold. Argue about per-relation distribution: Compare (27.6%), Evaluate-for (29.9%), Feature-of (11.3%) have double-digit violation rates with schema-informed prompt. The value proposition is per-relation guaranteed compliance, not overall statistical rate.\n77\t\n78\t### C2: \"Why not just post-hoc filter?\"\n79\t**Response (D013, 实验结果已出)**:\n80\t\n81\tPost-hoc filtering 实验结果：post-hoc F1 > OntoCoDec F1（SciERC 8.63 vs 8.36, DocRED 9.61 vs 8.24）——因 low F1 regime 下移除 FP 大幅提升 precision。\n82\t\n83\t**论文 framing（不以 F1 论高低，多维对比）**:\n84\t1. **Recall 维度（核心论点）**: OntoCoDec recall 上升 (SciERC +0.20pp, DocRED +0.56pp) = 概率质量重分配到合法 token 生效。Post-hoc recall 下降 (SciERC -0.72pp, DocRED -1.06pp) = 正确 triple 被误删。\n85\t2. **Information coverage**: DocRED post-hoc 丢弃 **48.1%** triples（近半数信息丢失），SciERC 16.8%。OntoCoDec 保留全部 triple slots。\n86\t3. **Operational**: OntoCoDec 产出即合规、无需后处理、支持流式。Post-hoc 需额外管线、不适用实时场景。\n87\t4. **Precision trade-off（诚实承认）**: \"Post-hoc achieves higher precision by removing a large fraction of triples, many of which are incorrect. This trades information coverage for precision — valid when FP are costly, but inadequate when completeness matters.\"\n88\t\n89\t数据表：SciERC post-hoc rejection 16.8%, OntoCoDec recall 11.60 vs post-hoc 10.68; DocRED post-hoc rejection 48.1%, OntoCoDec recall 10.02 vs post-hoc 8.40。\n90\t\n91\t**Reviewer 补充发现（D013 后）**:\n92\t5. **ET 残余**：post-hoc 只删 triples 不改 entity list，残余 ET=0.4% (SciERC) / 2.47% (DocRED)。OntoCoDec ET=0%。Post-hoc 无法解决 entity type 违规。\n93\t6. **127 个被删 TP (DocRED)**：过滤前 TP=1137，过滤后 TP=1010。丢失的 127 个 TP（11.2%）是正确提取但 entity type 违规的 triple。OntoCoDec 通过生成时强制合法 type 保留这些 TP——\"prevent vs detect\" 核心论据的具体数据。\n94\t7. **OntoCoDec+post-hoc 组合**（future work idea）：先 constrain 再 filter 残余 DR。低优先级，May 19 前不做。\n95\t\n96\t### C3: \"Bitwise AND of two masks is not novel\"\n97\t**Response**: The novelty is not the AND operation — it's (a) the automatic compilation from ontology definitions (zero-code schema compliance), (b) the stateful entity registry enabling cross-field constraints during autoregressive generation, (c) the decidability taxonomy providing theoretical guidance, and (d) the systematic violation landscape measurement motivating the approach.\n98\t\n99\t### C4: \"Evaluate-for violation rate increases with schema-informed prompt\"\n100\t**Response (prior-constraint conflict framework)**: Evaluate-for has 23/36 valid pairs; Method→Task is invalid for Evaluate-for but natural in the LLM's distributional prior (\"Method X evaluates for Task Y\" is semantically plausible). Schema-informed prompting creates a **prior-constraint conflict**: the model learns to avoid Method→Task for Evaluate-for (reducing count 133→87, -34.6%), but the remaining instances are harder boundary cases where the model's type assignment strategy becomes less stable. This is not just \"harder instances\" — it's an active interference between prompt-level constraint signals and the model's learned type associations.\n101\t\n102\t**This strengthens the paper's claim**: prompt-level intervention is not merely insufficient but potentially **counterproductive** for specific constraint configurations. Decoding-time enforcement avoids this issue entirely — it operates on logits, not on the model's reasoning process, so there is no prior-constraint conflict.\n103\t\n104\t### C5: \"Only tested on one model (Qwen3-8B)\"\n105\t**Response**: Cross-model validation DONE (D016 bootstrap verified). Llama-3.1-8B 零代码修改：\n106\t- SciERC: DR 13.34%→0.08% (↓99.4%), R-F1 -0.14pp (p=0.011, negligible), E-F1 NS\n107\t- DocRED: DR 26.07%→2.55% (↓90.2%), R-F1 +0.29pp (p=0.013, significant), E-F1 -0.64pp (p=0.022, modest decline)\n108\t- Parse failures: unconstrained 68 vs full_s1 91 (6.8% vs 9.1%)\n109\t\n110\t**Cross-model claim 指导（Reviewer 专项评估）**:\n111\t- ✅ 可声明：\"OntoCoDec generalizes across model families without code modification\"（程序性事实，铁证）\n112\t- ❌ 不可声明：\"consistently achieves the same reduction rate\"（仅 2 模型，不足以量化声明）\n113\t- **RV↓DR↑ 正交性 finding**: Llama RV baseline 低(16%) 但 DR baseline 高(26%)，反向于 Qwen。证明两层约束解决正交 failure modes——vocabulary compliance ≠ semantic compliance。应作为 §5 cross-model 独立 finding 展开。\n114\t- **Parse failure 偏差**: checker skip parse failures (不计入 F1)，Llama 68/998=6.8% vs Qwen 12/998=1.2%。偏差方向保守（不利于 constrained），不威胁 claim。但需 footnote 披露 + cross-model 表增加 parse failure rate 行。\n115\t- **Llama SciERC CF=6.56%**: 比 Qwen 同量级更高，non-local constraint 问题在 Llama 上更突出，limitations 提及。\n116\t- 等 llama_docred_full_s1 出来后定最终 claim 措辞。\n117\t\n118\t### C6: \"Constrained decoding degrades generation quality (CRANE, Structure Snowballing)\"\n119\t**Response**: OntoCoDec's semantic constraints are narrower than full grammar constraints — only type tokens are masked, free text is unconstrained. **Bootstrap CI (10000×, D012 Qwen + D016 Llama, all registry-aligned)**:\n120\t\n121\t**Qwen3-8B**: SciERC R-F1 +0.13pp (p=0.58, NS), E-F1 -0.03pp (NS). DocRED R-F1 +0.50pp (p<0.001), E-F1 +1.23pp (p<0.001).\n122\t**Llama-3.1-8B**: SciERC R-F1 -0.14pp (p=0.011, negligible), E-F1 NS. DocRED R-F1 +0.29pp (p=0.013), E-F1 -0.64pp (p=0.022).\n123\t\n124\t**Cross-model pattern**: DocRED R-F1 显著提升（两个模型）。E-F1 model-dependent（Qwen +1.23pp, Llama -0.64pp）。\n125\t- 机制：grammar 消除 OOV relation names + 非标 entity types → all_set 方法下减少 FP → precision 提升。Grammar 是 F1 提升的唯一来源（grammar_only Ent F1=59.38% ≈ full_s1 59.37%, Δ=0.01pp, p=0.66）。Semantic 层对 F1 无额外贡献。\n126\t- Frame as: \"On DocRED, R-F1 gains are significant for both models. Entity F1 impact is model-dependent.\"\n127\t- 不升级为 core claim，但如实报告。\n128\t\n129\t### C7: \"Your method trades DR violations for CF violations (cross-field consistency)\"\n130\t**Response**: Both S1 and S2 show elevated CF (per-triple rate ~8-10%). This is an inherent limitation of per-relation independent type enforcement. Must be proactively reported as a limitation. Defense:\n131\t\n132\t**CF 子类型分析（根因已确认）**：\n133\t- **EVR（entity-vs-relation type drift）**: 占 CF 的 >90%。同一 entity 在 entity list 和 relation triple 中被赋予不同 type。S1: 245 entities (7.34%), S2: 178 entities (5.54%, -27%)\n134\t- **Within-rel（同 entity 跨 relation type 不一致）**: S1: 10 (0.36%), S2: 18 (0.72%)\n135\t- S2 减少 EVR 但增加 within-rel——trade-off 更复杂，不是单纯好/差\n136\t\n137\t**Top 冲突模式**: Generic↔OtherScientificTerm (60次), Material↔OtherScientificTerm (28次), Material↔Method (20次)。**这些是 SciERC type system 固有的语义边界模糊区**——同一术语在不同学术语境下确实可以被合理归类为不同 type。CF 在相当程度上是 type system 模糊性的体现，非纯粹的方法缺陷。\n138\t\n139\t**论证层次**：\n140\t1. DR violations = structurally invalid triples（下游系统不可用）→ hard constraint\n141\t2. CF violations = same entity gets different types across relations → individual triples remain type-valid, only cross-triple consistency broken → soft preference\n142\t3. CF 的根因是 type system 语义边界模糊 + per-relation 独立 enforcement，非 bug\n143\t4. Future work: cross-relation global consistency pass (entity-level type consensus before relation-specific enforcement)\n144\t\n145\t**机制归因（口径对账确认）**：grammar_only CF=0.08%（与 unconstrained 持平），full_s1 CF=9.90%，full_s2 CF=8.03%。**CF 100% 由 semantic 层引入，grammar 层无贡献。** 这为 \"CF 是 semantic type enforcement 的系统性副作用\" 提供干净的消融证据。\n146\t\n147\t**论文数字口径**：CF rate 用 violation_checker 口径（denominator=total_entities，与 DR/RV/ET 一致）。分析段落额外给 entity-level EVR 率 + 受影响样本比例。注意：analyze_cf 脚本的 EVR/WR 两维度不是独立的（WR⊂EVR），论文中不要作为两个独立维度报告。\n148\t\n149\t**Do NOT hide this data.** Proactive disclosure + severity distinction + root cause analysis + type ambiguity evidence + 消融归因 = 最强防御策略。\n150\t\n151\t### C8: \"Absolute F1 is too low (~8%) — results are not meaningful\"\n152\t**Response**: This is a zero-shot extraction setting (no training data, no fine-tuning). Low F1 is expected — supervised SOTA on SciERC relation F1 is ~40-50%. Our contribution is the constraint enforcement method, not extraction quality. F1 is a control variable verifying constraints don't degrade quality, not an optimization target. Recommended framing: \"We evaluate in a zero-shot setting to demonstrate that our constraint enforcement method works without task-specific training. F1 is reported to verify that constraint enforcement does not degrade extraction quality, not as a claim of state-of-the-art performance.\"\n153\t\n154\t## Paper Structure (Draft)\n155\t1. Introduction: Violation landscape motivation + composable constraint framework overview\n156\t2. Background: Grammar-constrained decoding (XGrammar) + IE ontology structure\n157\t3. Violation Landscape Study (Phase 0 empirics — independent contribution)\n158\t4. OntoCoDec Framework: Compiler + TypeConstraintProcessor + S1/S2 strategies\n159\t5. Experiments: Constrained vs unconstrained vs post-hoc vs prompt-based\n160\t6. Related Work: 5 constraint paradigms (grammar, vocabulary, structural, type-checking, ontology)\n161\t7. Conclusion\n162\t\n163\t## Claim Calibration (per Reviewer assessment)\n164\t\n165\t**Safe to claim (sufficient evidence from Phase 2)**:\n166\t- \"First systematic study of ontology constraint violations in LLM-based IE\"\n167\t- \"Violation rate correlates with constraint tightness, not ontology size\" (D014: DR reduction ceiling 由 tightness × model RV baseline 共同决定)\n168\t- \"Grammar+semantic constrained decoding eliminates 94% of DR violations at zero F1 cost\" ✅ Phase 2 confirmed\n169\t- \"Two-layer architecture provides complementary coverage — grammar enables semantic\" ✅ Ablation confirmed\n170\t- \"Prompt-level intervention scales poorly with ontology complexity\" ✅ SciERC ↓62% vs DocRED ↓32%\n171\t\n172\t**Claim with caution**:\n173\t- \"Near-complete type-valid IE\" — S1 0.93%, S2 0.97% residual, not truly 0%. Title updated to \"Near-Complete\"\n174\t- \"Principled framework applicable to arbitrary IE ontologies\" — validated on 2 datasets + 1 model only\n175\t- \"F1 improvement\" — SciERC: not significant (p=0.58), frame as F1-neutral; DocRED: significant (+0.50pp, p<0.001), 可报告但不升级为 core claim，归因于 OOV elimination 而非约束解码本身的提升\n176\t- \"CF reveals type system ambiguity\" — 可在 §5.3 作为 analysis finding 展开（Generic↔OtherScientificTerm 等模式有独立 insight 价值），但 §7 必须同时保留 CF 作为 limitation + future work。**两处都要有，缺一不可。** 不能暗示\"因为是 type ambiguity 所以 CF 可接受\"\n177\t\n178\t**Do NOT claim**:\n179\t- \"General infrastructure for IE\" — only zero-shot extraction validated\n180\t- \"State-of-the-art\" — F1 is control variable, not optimization target (see C8)\n181\t- \"Synergistic effect\" — mechanism is enabling dependency, not mutual amplification (see Claim 3)\n182\t- \"S2 solves CF\" or \"S2 mitigates Structure Snowballing\" — data shows S2 ≈ S1 on all metrics; position as architectural variant only\n183\t- \"Pilot50 DR=0%\" — small-sample artifact, full S2 has DR=0.97%\n184\t- \"Grammar-first invariant\" 作为独立 claim — 证据不足（仅 1 次崩溃触发，实现是 fallback 非形式化保证）。写入 §4 方法论设计原则（1-2 句），不升级为 claim\n185\t- \"Robust dual-layer composition across schema complexities\" — 等 DocRED 完成。最终如 fallback ≤5/998，可写经验性陈述，不做泛化 claim\n186\t\n187\t## Risk Ranking (ordered by reject probability)\n188\t\n189\t1. **CF violation trade-off under-addressed** (MEDIUM-HIGH): S1 9.9%, S2 8.03% — both elevated. **S2 confirmed: does NOT solve CF.** This is the #1 attack surface. Mitigated by proactive disclosure + severity distinction + root cause analysis (C7). Must be reported as explicit limitation with future work direction (global entity-type consensus).\n190\t2. ~~**Single model limitation**~~ (RESOLVED): Llama-3.1-8B SciERC ✅ (DR↓99.4%) + DocRED ✅ (DR↓90.2%). 2 模型 × 2 数据集全矩阵完成。\n191\t3. **Novelty perception** (MEDIUM): \"PLDI'25 for code → OntoCoDec for IE\" attack line. Must argue IE constraint structure differs fundamentally.\n192\t4. ~~**DocRED Phase 2 weak**~~ (RESOLVED → reframed as D014): Qwen DR↓44.7%, Llama DR↓90.2% — both substantial. Weaker Qwen reduction explained by RV baseline interaction (D014), not method failure.\n193\t5. ~~**Phase 2 F1 drop**~~ (RESOLVED): F1 confirmed neutral (SciERC) or positive (DocRED, p<0.001). Bootstrap CI D012 confirms. No longer a risk.\n194\t\n195\t## Critical Path to EMNLP Submission (May 25)\n196\t\n197\t- **May 13-14**: Phase 0 + Phase 1 + Phase 2 SciERC ✅\n198\t- **May 14**: Phase 2 DocRED 4-way ablation ✅ + Llama SciERC cross-model ✅ + Dream 完成 (3/6)\n199\t- **May 14-15**: Llama DocRED 2 组实验 ✅ + Checker 修正 ✅ + post-hoc baseline ✅ + bootstrap CI ✅ + related work ✅\n200\t- **May 14-15**: D014 tightness claim 修订 + §5 cross-model subsection + abstract/conclusion 修正 (Agent 执行中)\n201\t- **May 15-17**: 全文校对 + Discussion 整合 + 最终数字确认\n202\t- **May 19**: 内部稿 → submit_paper_to_review\n203\t- **May 19-24**: Review 修改 + 最终提交\n204\t\n205\t**当前瓶颈**: 无技术 blocker。等 Reviewer 跨文件一致性审查 + 编译验证后即可 submit_paper_to_review。\n206\t\n207\t## Status\n208\t- Phase 0 SciERC: ✅ Complete (minimal + schema-informed)\n209\t- Phase 0 DocRED: ✅ Complete (minimal 18.7% DR + schema-informed 12.8% DR)\n210\t- Phase 1 Compiler: ✅ Complete (grammar + semantic layers integrated)\n211\t- Phase 2 SciERC (5 configs): ✅ Complete (S1 DR↓94% F1-neutral, S2 降级为 ablation)\n212\t- Phase 2 DocRED (4 configs): ✅ Complete (full_s1 DR↓45%, grammar ET/RV→0%)\n213\t- Llama SciERC cross-model: ✅ Complete (DR↓99.4%, F1-neutral, 零代码修改)\n214\t- Llama DocRED cross-model: ✅ Complete (full_s1 DR↓90.2%, unconstrained DR=26.07%)\n215\t- Checker v2 (D011): ✅ Fixed (ET triple-counting → unique entity dedup)\n216\t- Bootstrap CI (D012): ✅ Fixed + confirmed (entity filter bug resolved)\n217\t- Post-hoc baseline (D013): ✅ Complete (multi-dimensional framing)\n218\t- Related work: ✅ 42 bib entries, 4 additions merged\n219\t- Dream 6/6 actions: ✅ All complete\n220\t- CF violation analysis: ✅ Confirmed inherent limitation (S1 9.9% SciERC / 2.57% DocRED / 12.02% Llama DocRED)\n221\t- D014 tightness revision: ✅ Complete (tightness × RV baseline dual-factor)\n222\t- Llama bootstrap CI (D016): ✅ Fixed + verified (registry-aligned ≤0.05pp, all p-values in paper)\n223\t- Paper compilation: ✅ 8 pages正文 + appendix\n224\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"175080ca-6504-4947-a884-b89f355ed917","uuid":"08cc1769-6a06-4b10-821c-3116ac859ce6","timestamp":"2026-05-16T02:27:11.324Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_6/projects/schema_semantic_constrained_ie/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260516T021434/best/paper_framing.md","content":"# OntoCoDec — Paper Framing\n\n## Target Venue\nEMNLP 2026 (ARR submission May 25, 2026)\n\n## Title\nOntoCoDec: Type-Valid Information Extraction via Compiled Ontology Constraints\n(D015: \"Near-Complete\" dropped — DocRED residual DR=10.21% (Qwen) 不算 near-complete。论文贡献是方法，不是特定消除率。SciERC 0.93% 和 DocRED 2.55% (Llama) 可在正文中描述为 near-complete，但 title 不宜 overclaim。)\n\n## Core Insight\nLLM-based IE systems produce systematic ontology constraint violations concentrated in specific relation types. Prompt-level intervention (schema-informed prompting) reduces violations by ~62% but cannot eliminate them — certain relation types retain 25-30% violation rates even with explicit constraint descriptions. OntoCoDec provides **near-complete elimination (DR 15.4%→0.93%, ↓94%) at zero or positive F1 impact** through automatic ontology-to-decoder constraint compilation with two complementary layers.\n\n**Phase 2 confirmed (D012 bootstrap CI, v2 fix)**: Grammar+Semantic dual-layer constrained decoding reduces domain/range violations by 94%, eliminates entity-type and relation-vocabulary violations entirely (→0%). F1 impact is **dataset-dependent**:\n- SciERC: Rel F1 neutral (+0.13pp, p=0.58), Ent F1 neutral (-0.03pp, p=0.53)\n- DocRED: Rel F1 **significantly improved** (+0.50pp, p<0.001, 95% CI [+0.23, +0.81]); Ent F1 **significantly improved** (+1.23pp, p<0.001, 95% CI [+0.94, +1.55])\n- Mechanism: grammar 消除 OOV relation names (DocRED RV 29.66%→0.03%) + 非标 entity types (ET 2.48%→0%)。all_set F1 方法下 OOV=FP → fewer FP → higher precision/F1。SciERC baseline RV/ET 已很低，效果不显著。\n- **Grammar 层是 F1 提升的唯一来源**: grammar_only Ent F1=59.38% ≈ full_s1 59.37% (Δ+0.01pp, p=0.66)。Semantic 层对 F1 无额外贡献，专注 DR reduction。\n\n## Core Claims\n\n### Claim 1 (Empirical): Violation Landscape\nLLM-based IE systems violate ontology type constraints at non-trivial rates (15.4% per-triple on SciERC, 18.7% on DocRED). Violations are **not uniformly distributed** — they concentrate on relation types with tight domain/range constraints (Feature-of 33.5%, Compare 42.4%) while loose-constraint relations show near-zero violation (Used-for 0.8%).\n\n**Key insight**: Violation rate is driven by **constraint tightness**, not ontology size. A small ontology with tight constraints can produce more violations than a large ontology with loose constraints.\n\n**D014 修订**: DR reduction ceiling 由 **tightness × model RV baseline** 共同决定，非 tightness 单因素。Llama DocRED DR↓90.2% vs Qwen DR↓44.7%（同一 ontology τ̄=0.842）。机制：Qwen RV=29.66% >> Llama RV=16.03% → grammar 层将 OOV triples 强制匹配有效关系名 → 揭露大量 latent DR violations → 残余 DR 更高。这是比单一 tightness 更深的 insight。\n\n**Evidence**: SciERC (7 relations) 15.4%; DocRED (96 relations) 18.7% — comparable rates despite 14× ontology size difference. Schema-informed prompt on DocRED only achieves DR↓32% (vs SciERC ↓62%), confirming **prompt-level intervention scales poorly with ontology complexity**.\n\n### Claim 2 (Empirical): Prompt Insufficiency\nSchema-informed prompting (explicitly describing domain/range constraints in the prompt) reduces but does not eliminate violations:\n- Overall: 15.4% → 5.78% (-62.4%), still above 5%\n- Per-relation: Compare 42.4% → 27.6%, Evaluate-for 24.1% → 29.9% (**worse**)\n- Prompt intervention is unreliable at the per-relation level — some relations improve, one regresses\n\n**Narrative**: This is NOT about \"5.78% barely above 5%\". The story is: **prompt-level intervention is fundamentally unreliable as a guarantee mechanism**. It works statistically but cannot provide per-instance compliance. Three specific relation types retain >10% violation rates with schema-informed prompts. For safety-critical IE (biomedical, legal, regulatory), statistical reduction is insufficient — guaranteed compliance is required.\n\n### Claim 3 (Methodological): Composable Constraint Framework\nOntoCoDec automatically compiles IE ontology schemas into two composable constraint layers:\n1. **Grammar layer** (XGrammar): JSON structure + type vocabulary constraints (CFG-expressible)\n2. **Semantic layer** (TypeConstraintProcessor): Cross-field domain/range constraints via stateful entity registry + dynamic logit masking\n\nThe two layers are **complementary with enabling dependency**: grammar ensures every generated relation type is in the valid vocabulary, which enables the semantic layer to look up and enforce domain/range rules for that type. Without grammar, the semantic layer encounters unknown relation types and cannot enforce constraints (explaining why semantic_only achieves only ↓24% vs full_s1 ↓94%). This is NOT \"synergistic\" (mutual amplification) — grammar is a prerequisite for semantic, not vice versa.\n\nThe two layers compose via bitwise AND of token masks. Recommended framing: \"Grammar and semantic constraints compose via bitwise AND with an enabling dependency: grammar ensures structural validity, enabling semantic constraints to enforce domain/range rules. When constraint tightness creates empty intersection between layers, the system degrades gracefully to grammar-only constraints, maintaining structural validity as a guaranteed floor.\"\n\n**Graceful degradation + Fallback 频率量化** (D008 + Reviewer 发现):\nWhen $M_{semantic} \\cap M_{grammar} = \\emptyset$, the system falls back to grammar-only control.\n\n**关键量化数据（Reviewer 从日志挖掘）**:\n- Llama DocRED full_s1: **32,921 次 fallback / 577 docs = ~57 次/doc**\n- Llama SciERC full_s1: **5,882 次 fallback / 550 docs = ~10.7 次/doc**\n- DocRED fallback 频率是 SciERC 的 **5.3×**\n- Qwen DocRED fallback 率未知（日志当时无 fallback logging，需估算）\n\n**这直接解释了 DocRED DR 残余 10.19% vs SciERC 0.93%**: 更多 token 位置退化为 grammar-only → grammar-only 的 DR 已知为 26.17% → 高 fallback = 高残余 DR。\n\n**论文建议**: 在 §5 tightness 段报告 fallback 率，定义 \"Constraint Coverage\" 指标（semantic masking 实际生效的 token 比例）。这把 \"10.19% DR 残余\" 从弱点变成可量化分析的 finding。Frame as \"engineering robustness\" in §4; fallback 频率 + tightness 作为 §5 定量分析。\n\n**Decidability taxonomy**: Constraints classified by prefix-decidability:\n- (a) Purely local: entity type ∈ vocabulary (grammar layer)\n- (b) Prefix-decidable with state: relation argument types compatible with domain/range (semantic layer, requires entity registry)\n- (c) Truly non-local: forward coreference — out of scope for forward-only decoding\n\n### Claim 4 (Methodological): S1 vs S2 Decoding Strategies — Architectural Ablation\n- S1 (single-pass): Both layers applied throughout generation. **Recommended primary strategy** — simpler, slightly better metrics across the board.\n- S2 (two-pass): Pass 1 extracts entities (grammar-only), Pass 2 generates relations with input-dependent grammar compiled from Pass 1 entities.\n\n**S2 full results (551/551 SciERC)**: DR 0.97% (vs S1 0.93%), CF 8.03% (vs S1 9.9%), R-F1 8.03% (vs S1 8.36%). S2 does NOT solve CF — the 1.87pp reduction is not significant. S2 also slightly worse on DR and F1. **S2 is an architectural variant demonstrating framework flexibility, not a CF solution.** Position in paper as ablation (Section 5 or Appendix), not as a core contribution.\n\n⚠️ **Do NOT cite pilot50 DR=0% as S2 evidence** — small-sample artifact; full run shows DR=0.97%. Per-relation S2 DR is worse than S1 on Compare (4.6% vs 2.82%), Part-of (1.25% vs 0%), Used-for (0.12% vs 0%).\n\n## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns\n\n### C1: \"5.78% is barely above 5% — threshold is arbitrary\"\n**Response**: Don't argue about the threshold. Argue about per-relation distribution: Compare (27.6%), Evaluate-for (29.9%), Feature-of (11.3%) have double-digit violation rates with schema-informed prompt. The value proposition is per-relation guaranteed compliance, not overall statistical rate.\n\n### C2: \"Why not just post-hoc filter?\"\n**Response (D013, 实验结果已出)**:\n\nPost-hoc filtering 实验结果：post-hoc F1 > OntoCoDec F1（SciERC 8.63 vs 8.36, DocRED 9.61 vs 8.24）——因 low F1 regime 下移除 FP 大幅提升 precision。\n\n**论文 framing（不以 F1 论高低，多维对比）**:\n1. **Recall 维度（核心论点）**: OntoCoDec recall 上升 (SciERC +0.20pp, DocRED +0.56pp) = 概率质量重分配到合法 token 生效。Post-hoc recall 下降 (SciERC -0.72pp, DocRED -1.06pp) = 正确 triple 被误删。\n2. **Information coverage**: DocRED post-hoc 丢弃 **48.1%** triples（近半数信息丢失），SciERC 16.8%。OntoCoDec 保留全部 triple slots。\n3. **Operational**: OntoCoDec 产出即合规、无需后处理、支持流式。Post-hoc 需额外管线、不适用实时场景。\n4. **Precision trade-off（诚实承认）**: \"Post-hoc achieves higher precision by removing a large fraction of triples, many of which are incorrect. This trades information coverage for precision — valid when FP are costly, but inadequate when completeness matters.\"\n\n数据表：SciERC post-hoc rejection 16.8%, OntoCoDec recall 11.60 vs post-hoc 10.68; DocRED post-hoc rejection 48.1%, OntoCoDec recall 10.02 vs post-hoc 8.40。\n\n**Reviewer 补充发现（D013 后）**:\n5. **ET 残余**：post-hoc 只删 triples 不改 entity list，残余 ET=0.4% (SciERC) / 2.47% (DocRED)。OntoCoDec ET=0%。Post-hoc 无法解决 entity type 违规。\n6. **127 个被删 TP (DocRED)**：过滤前 TP=1137，过滤后 TP=1010。丢失的 127 个 TP（11.2%）是正确提取但 entity type 违规的 triple。OntoCoDec 通过生成时强制合法 type 保留这些 TP——\"prevent vs detect\" 核心论据的具体数据。\n7. **OntoCoDec+post-hoc 组合**（future work idea）：先 constrain 再 filter 残余 DR。低优先级，May 19 前不做。\n\n### C3: \"Bitwise AND of two masks is not novel\"\n**Response**: The novelty is not the AND operation — it's (a) the automatic compilation from ontology definitions (zero-code schema compliance), (b) the stateful entity registry enabling cross-field constraints during autoregressive generation, (c) the decidability taxonomy providing theoretical guidance, and (d) the systematic violation landscape measurement motivating the approach.\n\n### C4: \"Evaluate-for violation rate increases with schema-informed prompt\"\n**Response (prior-constraint conflict framework)**: Evaluate-for has 23/36 valid pairs; Method→Task is invalid for Evaluate-for but natural in the LLM's distributional prior (\"Method X evaluates for Task Y\" is semantically plausible). Schema-informed prompting creates a **prior-constraint conflict**: the model learns to avoid Method→Task for Evaluate-for (reducing count 133→87, -34.6%), but the remaining instances are harder boundary cases where the model's type assignment strategy becomes less stable. This is not just \"harder instances\" — it's an active interference between prompt-level constraint signals and the model's learned type associations.\n\n**This strengthens the paper's claim**: prompt-level intervention is not merely insufficient but potentially **counterproductive** for specific constraint configurations. Decoding-time enforcement avoids this issue entirely — it operates on logits, not on the model's reasoning process, so there is no prior-constraint conflict.\n\n### C5: \"Only tested on one model (Qwen3-8B)\"\n**Response**: Cross-model validation DONE (D016 bootstrap verified). Llama-3.1-8B 零代码修改：\n- SciERC: DR 13.34%→0.08% (↓99.4%), R-F1 -0.14pp (p=0.011, negligible), E-F1 NS\n- DocRED: DR 26.07%→2.55% (↓90.2%), R-F1 +0.29pp (p=0.013, significant), E-F1 -0.64pp (p=0.022, modest decline)\n- Parse failures: unconstrained 68 vs full_s1 91 (6.8% vs 9.1%)\n\n**Cross-model claim 指导（Reviewer 专项评估）**:\n- ✅ 可声明：\"OntoCoDec generalizes across model families without code modification\"（程序性事实，铁证）\n- ❌ 不可声明：\"consistently achieves the same reduction rate\"（仅 2 模型，不足以量化声明）\n- **RV↓DR↑ 正交性 finding**: Llama RV baseline 低(16%) 但 DR baseline 高(26%)，反向于 Qwen。证明两层约束解决正交 failure modes——vocabulary compliance ≠ semantic compliance。应作为 §5 cross-model 独立 finding 展开。\n- **Parse failure 偏差**: checker skip parse failures (不计入 F1)，Llama 68/998=6.8% vs Qwen 12/998=1.2%。偏差方向保守（不利于 constrained），不威胁 claim。但需 footnote 披露 + cross-model 表增加 parse failure rate 行。\n- **Llama SciERC CF=6.56%**: 比 Qwen 同量级更高，non-local constraint 问题在 Llama 上更突出，limitations 提及。\n- 等 llama_docred_full_s1 出来后定最终 claim 措辞。\n\n### C6: \"Constrained decoding degrades generation quality (CRANE, Structure Snowballing)\"\n**Response**: OntoCoDec's semantic constraints are narrower than full grammar constraints — only type tokens are masked, free text is unconstrained. **Bootstrap CI (10000×, D012 Qwen + D016 Llama, all registry-aligned)**:\n\n**Qwen3-8B**: SciERC R-F1 +0.13pp (p=0.58, NS), E-F1 -0.03pp (NS). DocRED R-F1 +0.50pp (p<0.001), E-F1 +1.23pp (p<0.001).\n**Llama-3.1-8B**: SciERC R-F1 -0.14pp (p=0.011, negligible), E-F1 NS. DocRED R-F1 +0.29pp (p=0.013), E-F1 -0.64pp (p=0.022).\n\n**Cross-model pattern**: DocRED R-F1 显著提升（两个模型）。E-F1 model-dependent（Qwen +1.23pp, Llama -0.64pp）。\n- 机制：grammar 消除 OOV relation names + 非标 entity types → all_set 方法下减少 FP → precision 提升。Grammar 是 F1 提升的唯一来源（grammar_only Ent F1=59.38% ≈ full_s1 59.37%, Δ=0.01pp, p=0.66）。Semantic 层对 F1 无额外贡献。\n- Frame as: \"On DocRED, R-F1 gains are significant for both models. Entity F1 impact is model-dependent.\"\n- 不升级为 core claim，但如实报告。\n\n### C7: \"Your method trades DR violations for CF violations (cross-field consistency)\"\n**Response**: Both S1 and S2 show elevated CF (per-triple rate ~8-10%). This is an inherent limitation of per-relation independent type enforcement. Must be proactively reported as a limitation. Defense:\n\n**CF 子类型分析（根因已确认）**：\n- **EVR（entity-vs-relation type drift）**: 占 CF 的 >90%。同一 entity 在 entity list 和 relation triple 中被赋予不同 type。S1: 245 entities (7.34%), S2: 178 entities (5.54%, -27%)\n- **Within-rel（同 entity 跨 relation type 不一致）**: S1: 10 (0.36%), S2: 18 (0.72%)\n- S2 减少 EVR 但增加 within-rel——trade-off 更复杂，不是单纯好/差\n\n**Top 冲突模式**: Generic↔OtherScientificTerm (60次), Material↔OtherScientificTerm (28次), Material↔Method (20次)。**这些是 SciERC type system 固有的语义边界模糊区**——同一术语在不同学术语境下确实可以被合理归类为不同 type。CF 在相当程度上是 type system 模糊性的体现，非纯粹的方法缺陷。\n\n**论证层次**：\n1. DR violations = structurally invalid triples（下游系统不可用）→ hard constraint\n2. CF violations = same entity gets different types across relations → individual triples remain type-valid, only cross-triple consistency broken → soft preference\n3. CF 的根因是 type system 语义边界模糊 + per-relation 独立 enforcement，非 bug\n4. Future work: cross-relation global consistency pass (entity-level type consensus before relation-specific enforcement)\n\n**机制归因（口径对账确认）**：grammar_only CF=0.08%（与 unconstrained 持平），full_s1 CF=9.90%，full_s2 CF=8.03%。**CF 100% 由 semantic 层引入，grammar 层无贡献。** 这为 \"CF 是 semantic type enforcement 的系统性副作用\" 提供干净的消融证据。\n\n**论文数字口径**：CF rate 用 violation_checker 口径（denominator=total_entities，与 DR/RV/ET 一致）。分析段落额外给 entity-level EVR 率 + 受影响样本比例。注意：analyze_cf 脚本的 EVR/WR 两维度不是独立的（WR⊂EVR），论文中不要作为两个独立维度报告。\n\n**Do NOT hide this data.** Proactive disclosure + severity distinction + root cause analysis + type ambiguity evidence + 消融归因 = 最强防御策略。\n\n### C8: \"Absolute F1 is too low (~8%) — results are not meaningful\"\n**Response**: This is a zero-shot extraction setting (no training data, no fine-tuning). Low F1 is expected — supervised SOTA on SciERC relation F1 is ~40-50%. Our contribution is the constraint enforcement method, not extraction quality. F1 is a control variable verifying constraints don't degrade quality, not an optimization target. Recommended framing: \"We evaluate in a zero-shot setting to demonstrate that our constraint enforcement method works without task-specific training. F1 is reported to verify that constraint enforcement does not degrade extraction quality, not as a claim of state-of-the-art performance.\"\n\n## Paper Structure (Draft)\n1. Introduction: Violation landscape motivation + composable constraint framework overview\n2. Background: Grammar-constrained decoding (XGrammar) + IE ontology structure\n3. Violation Landscape Study (Phase 0 empirics — independent contribution)\n4. OntoCoDec Framework: Compiler + TypeConstraintProcessor + S1/S2 strategies\n5. Experiments: Constrained vs unconstrained vs post-hoc vs prompt-based\n6. Related Work: 5 constraint paradigms (grammar, vocabulary, structural, type-checking, ontology)\n7. Conclusion\n\n## Claim Calibration (per Reviewer assessment)\n\n**Safe to claim (sufficient evidence from Phase 2)**:\n- \"First systematic study of ontology constraint violations in LLM-based IE\"\n- \"Violation rate correlates with constraint tightness, not ontology size\" (D014: DR reduction ceiling 由 tightness × model RV baseline 共同决定)\n- \"Grammar+semantic constrained decoding eliminates 94% of DR violations at zero F1 cost\" ✅ Phase 2 confirmed\n- \"Two-layer architecture provides complementary coverage — grammar enables semantic\" ✅ Ablation confirmed\n- \"Prompt-level intervention scales poorly with ontology complexity\" ✅ SciERC ↓62% vs DocRED ↓32%\n\n**Claim with caution**:\n- \"Near-complete type-valid IE\" — S1 0.93%, S2 0.97% residual, not truly 0%. Title updated to \"Near-Complete\"\n- \"Principled framework applicable to arbitrary IE ontologies\" — validated on 2 datasets + 1 model only\n- \"F1 improvement\" — SciERC: not significant (p=0.58), frame as F1-neutral; DocRED: significant (+0.50pp, p<0.001), 可报告但不升级为 core claim，归因于 OOV elimination 而非约束解码本身的提升\n- \"CF reveals type system ambiguity\" — 可在 §5.3 作为 analysis finding 展开（Generic↔OtherScientificTerm 等模式有独立 insight 价值），但 §7 必须同时保留 CF 作为 limitation + future work。**两处都要有，缺一不可。** 不能暗示\"因为是 type ambiguity 所以 CF 可接受\"\n\n**Do NOT claim**:\n- \"General infrastructure for IE\" — only zero-shot extraction validated\n- \"State-of-the-art\" — F1 is control variable, not optimization target (see C8)\n- \"Synergistic effect\" — mechanism is enabling dependency, not mutual amplification (see Claim 3)\n- \"S2 solves CF\" or \"S2 mitigates Structure Snowballing\" — data shows S2 ≈ S1 on all metrics; position as architectural variant only\n- \"Pilot50 DR=0%\" — small-sample artifact, full S2 has DR=0.97%\n- \"Grammar-first invariant\" 作为独立 claim — 证据不足（仅 1 次崩溃触发，实现是 fallback 非形式化保证）。写入 §4 方法论设计原则（1-2 句），不升级为 claim\n- \"Robust dual-layer composition across schema complexities\" — 等 DocRED 完成。最终如 fallback ≤5/998，可写经验性陈述，不做泛化 claim\n\n## Risk Ranking (ordered by reject probability)\n\n1. **CF violation trade-off under-addressed** (MEDIUM-HIGH): S1 9.9%, S2 8.03% — both elevated. **S2 confirmed: does NOT solve CF.** This is the #1 attack surface. Mitigated by proactive disclosure + severity distinction + root cause analysis (C7). Must be reported as explicit limitation with future work direction (global entity-type consensus).\n2. ~~**Single model limitation**~~ (RESOLVED): Llama-3.1-8B SciERC ✅ (DR↓99.4%) + DocRED ✅ (DR↓90.2%). 2 模型 × 2 数据集全矩阵完成。\n3. **Novelty perception** (MEDIUM): \"PLDI'25 for code → OntoCoDec for IE\" attack line. Must argue IE constraint structure differs fundamentally.\n4. ~~**DocRED Phase 2 weak**~~ (RESOLVED → reframed as D014): Qwen DR↓44.7%, Llama DR↓90.2% — both substantial. Weaker Qwen reduction explained by RV baseline interaction (D014), not method failure.\n5. ~~**Phase 2 F1 drop**~~ (RESOLVED): F1 confirmed neutral (SciERC) or positive (DocRED, p<0.001). Bootstrap CI D012 confirms. No longer a risk.\n\n## Critical Path to EMNLP Submission (May 25)\n\n- **May 13-14**: Phase 0 + Phase 1 + Phase 2 SciERC ✅\n- **May 14**: Phase 2 DocRED 4-way ablation ✅ + Llama SciERC cross-model ✅ + Dream 完成 (3/6)\n- **May 14-15**: Llama DocRED 2 组实验 ✅ + Checker 修正 ✅ + post-hoc baseline ✅ + bootstrap CI ✅ + related work ✅\n- **May 14-15**: D014 tightness claim 修订 + §5 cross-model subsection + abstract/conclusion 修正 (Agent 执行中)\n- **May 15-17**: 全文校对 + Discussion 整合 + 最终数字确认\n- **May 19**: 内部稿 → submit_paper_to_review\n- **May 19-24**: Review 修改 + 最终提交\n\n**当前瓶颈**: 无技术 blocker。等 Reviewer 跨文件一致性审查 + 编译验证后即可 submit_paper_to_review。\n\n## Status\n- Phase 0 SciERC: ✅ Complete (minimal + schema-informed)\n- Phase 0 DocRED: ✅ Complete (minimal 18.7% DR + schema-informed 12.8% DR)\n- Phase 1 Compiler: ✅ Complete (grammar + semantic layers integrated)\n- Phase 2 SciERC (5 configs): ✅ Complete (S1 DR↓94% F1-neutral, S2 降级为 ablation)\n- Phase 2 DocRED (4 configs): ✅ Complete (full_s1 DR↓45%, grammar ET/RV→0%)\n- Llama SciERC cross-model: ✅ Complete (DR↓99.4%, F1-neutral, 零代码修改)\n- Llama DocRED cross-model: ✅ Complete (full_s1 DR↓90.2%, unconstrained DR=26.07%)\n- Checker v2 (D011): ✅ Fixed (ET triple-counting → unique entity dedup)\n- Bootstrap CI (D012): ✅ Fixed + confirmed (entity filter bug resolved)\n- Post-hoc baseline (D013): ✅ Complete (multi-dimensional framing)\n- Related work: ✅ 42 bib entries, 4 additions merged\n- Dream 6/6 actions: ✅ All complete\n- CF violation analysis: ✅ Confirmed inherent limitation (S1 9.9% SciERC / 2.57% DocRED / 12.02% Llama DocRED)\n- D014 tightness revision: ✅ Complete (tightness × RV baseline dual-factor)\n- Llama bootstrap CI (D016): ✅ Fixed + verified (registry-aligned ≤0.05pp, all p-values in paper)\n- Paper compilation: ✅ 8 pages正文 + appendix\n","numLines":224,"startLine":1,"totalLines":224}}}
